  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/11-gymnotiformes-knifefishes-of-the-new-world/sternarchogiton-preto-2/",
      "html": "<p>The species grows to a length of 20–25 cm.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/11-gymnotiformes-knifefishes-of-the-new-world/sternarchogiton-preto-2/",
      "html": "<p>This black knifefish is imported from Peru.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/11-gymnotiformes-knifefishes-of-the-new-world/sternarchogiton-preto-2/",
      "html": "<p>Most probably these fish feed in the wild on land insects that fall into the water.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/11-gymnotiformes-knifefishes-of-the-new-world/sternarchogiton-preto-2/",
      "html": "<p>Aquarium observations show clearly that this knifefish tends to swim near the water surface. They often take air and water in the mouth; the water is then spat out in the form of a small blast. Like most knifefish these animals are very intelligent and observing them is extremely interesting.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/11-gymnotiformes-knifefishes-of-the-new-world/sternarchogiton-preto-2/",
      "html": "<p>Most probably this importation of this black knifefish from Peru (\"preto\" means \"black\") is the first one to Europe. The uniform black coloration is a good feature to distinguish the species from other members of the genus (there are five species of Sternarchogiton known so far).</p><p>However, a light stripe over the back is visible in many pictures. This is not a true coloration, but an effect of the light. The mucus of the fish is obviously very thick over the back, which is the reason for that light stripe.</p>"
    }
  ],
